{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  task 0003 (Task 3, custom code) — "Why Growers Choose Flora Bella"
  ============================================================================
  Task 3 originally shipped as 100% native block composition (see 0003_task3_howto.md) —
  DXB later asked for the same genuine custom-code exercise given to Tasks 4/5/6. This is
  that build.

  NOTE: this comment deliberately never spells out the Liquid tag delimiters for the
  schema, stylesheet, or javascript blocks below (plain words are used instead) — see the
  2026-09-06 lesson in this project's self_improve/LESSONS.md.

  WHAT THIS FILE NEEDS ALONGSIDE IT:
    - blocks/bfbella-benefit-card.liquid   (0003_task3_bfbella-benefit-card.liquid)
  Each card block renders itself entirely — this section only does
  `{% content_for 'blocks' %}`. Built this way from the start (unlike Tasks 4/5/6's first
  attempt) because a theme block referenced from an external blocks/*.liquid file cannot be
  read as data from its parent section — confirmed live via Task 4's bug in this same task
  series (block.type reports as the literal string "@theme" at runtime, not its declared
  name, and .settings reads from outside the block's own render come back blank). See
  .claude/CLAUDE.md's "Theme Blocks Must Render Themselves" section for the full rule.

  ICONS: production uses six lucide icons (Leaf, FileStack, Flag, Sparkles, Bug, Users)
  with no exact match in this theme's native icon set — hand-drawn inline SVGs for all six
  live in blocks/bfbella-benefit-card.liquid, verified by rendering them standalone first.

  HOVER ANIMATION: skipped when this section first shipped as native blocks (DXB's call,
  citing cost/risk of scoping shared-file CSS). That specific cost doesn't apply to custom
  code — a card lift + border glow, image zoom, and icon badge scale+rotate are a handful
  of `:hover` rules fully scoped to this section's own classes, zero shared-file risk. So
  they're included here. Flagging this clearly since it wasn't explicitly re-requested —
  easy to strip out if not wanted.

  CONTENT: zero real copy hardcoded — heading, subheading, and every card field are blank
  native settings/block fields until DXB fills them in. See 0003_task3_howto.md for the
  exact production text (still accurate) and 0003_task3_custom_howto.md (companion to this
  file) for where each piece goes in this custom version specifically.

  COLOR: no hardcoded hex. Accent (icon badges) resolves through
  `section.settings.accent_color`, falling back to the theme's own `color_palette.color3`.
  Background resolves through `section.settings.background_color`, falling back to
  `color_palette.color9` — confirmed via config/settings_data.json to be an exact match for
  production's #0a0a0a, same finding as the original native howto doc. Both are exposed to
  the self-rendering card block via CSS custom properties (`--bfbella-accent`,
  `--bfbella-bg`) set on this section's own root element, since Liquid variables can't cross
  into a block's own render the way section.settings can't be read from it either.

  MEDIA: two images in production are Pexels stock photos, not Shopify Files (the section's
  background texture, and card 6's "Handled with Care" photo) — per this project's media
  rule these can't be bundled by Claude. Both are optional/have a safe fallback (solid
  background color; card 6 renders fine with the icon+gradient alone if no image is set) —
  see 0003_task3_custom_howto.md for exactly which image DXB needs to source, and the five
  that are already Shopify Files DXB can pick directly.

  DEPLOY: save as sections/bfbella-why-choose.liquid in the live theme. DXB applies this —
  Claude never commits or touches the live repo.
  ============================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign accent = section.settings.accent_color | default: settings.color_palette.color3
  assign bg = section.settings.background_color | default: settings.color_palette.color9

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id, skip_contrast: true
  endif
%}

<div
  id="WhyChoose-{{ section.id }}"
  class="bfbella-why-choose{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  style="
    --bfbella-accent: {{ accent }};
    --bfbella-bg: {{ bg }};
    {% if section.settings.padding_top != blank %}--bfbella-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;{% endif %}
    {% if section.settings.padding_bottom != blank %}--bfbella-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;{% endif %}
  "
>
  {%- if section.settings.texture_image != blank -%}
    <div class="bfbella-why-choose__texture" aria-hidden="true">
      {{
        section.settings.texture_image
        | image_url: width: 1920
        | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '', class: 'bfbella-why-choose__texture-img'
      }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="bfbella-why-choose__inner page-width">

    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank or section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
      <div class="bfbella-why-choose__intro">
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="bfbella-why-choose__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="bfbella-why-choose__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="bfbella-why-choose__grid">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bfbella-why-choose {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block-start: var(--bfbella-pad-top, 8rem);
    padding-block-end: var(--bfbella-pad-bottom, 8rem);
    background-color: var(--bfbella-bg);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__texture {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    opacity: 0.05;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__texture-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__intro {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block-end: 5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__heading {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-block-end: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__subheading {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.6);
  }

  .bfbella-why-choose__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bfbella-why-choose * {
      transition: none !important;
      animation: none !important;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BFBella — Why Choose",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "bfbella-benefit-card"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subheading"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Used for the icon badges. Leave blank to use the theme's existing color3 (brand green) swatch."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Background color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the theme's existing color9 swatch — an exact match for production's near-black background."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "texture_image",
      "label": "Background texture image",
      "info": "Optional. Rendered at 5% opacity as a subtle full-bleed texture, matching production. The section looks correct without one — this is a nice-to-have layer, not load-bearing."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 128
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 128
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "BFBella — Why Choose",
      "category": "Custom",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" },
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" },
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" },
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" },
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" },
        { "type": "bfbella-benefit-card" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
